Methodology

The project followed a structured analytical workflow.

1. Data Cleaning (SQL)

The raw dataset was imported into MySQL and cleaned before statistical analysis.

The data cleaning process included:

Validating imported records.
Identifying and removing duplicate records.
Checking for invalid age values.
Verifying variable categories.
Preparing the cleaned dataset for statistical analysis.

SQL aggregate functions such as COUNT(), GROUP BY, ORDER BY, MIN(), MAX(), and AVG() were used to summarize and validate the dataset.

2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

