Key Findings

The analysis identified several factors associated with appointment attendance.

Key findings include:

Older patients were more likely to attend appointments.
Patients with hypertension demonstrated different attendance patterns than patients without hypertension.
Awaiting Time was an important predictor of appointment attendance.
Behavioural characteristics such as smoking and alcoholism were associated with appointment attendance.
Scholarship status was independently associated with appointment attendance.
Binary Logistic Regression identified independent predictors after adjusting for multiple demographic and clinical variables.
